{
  "description": "Every backend HTTP route, phone operation, phone protocol message and desktop window request (Electron `gofer:*` IPC), mapped to the CLI command that covers it or a named exclusion. tests/unit/test_cli_parity.py fails when one has neither. `api` means only the generic `Raticode api` command reaches it.",
  "exclusions": {
    "window-ui": "Serves the desktop window's own screens: attachments, media and link previews, voice input, the studio editor, generation jobs, themes, its terminal, clipboard, logs and developer tools. Scripts edit workflow.rattish and use `Raticode rattish` instead.",
    "desktop-auth": "Desktop security handshakes (path grants, trusted roots, the window's session token). A CLI that could call them could grant itself folder access.",
    "folder-approval": "Registers or opens a folder, which the backend only accepts with a folder approval from the desktop. Do it in the app; the CLI then works with the result.",
    "pairing": "Pairing and device actions require the Settings UI by design.",
    "provider-sign-in": "Provider sign-in opens an interactive browser login. Sign in on the machine itself with the provider's own CLI.",
    "credentials": "Stores account credentials or secret values. Credentials never go through CLI arguments; set them in the app.",
    "org-run-control": "Starts, pauses or resumes an organization or its heartbeats, or decides a consent request. Needs the user's separate authorization, so it stays in the Organizations tab.",
    "consent-gated": "The backend asks for the user's consent in the app before this change (archive, routines, webhooks, ingress, GitHub import, and restoring a revision, which can bring back full access). Kept in the app so consent is reviewed where it is shown.",
    "runs-agents": "Starts or steers agent work outside a workflow run (swarm start/control/messages, organization wake, launches, checks, retries). Not offered by the CLI; start this work in the app.",
    "worker-tools": "Used by an organization employee during its own run (claims, artifacts, memory). Not a user action.",
    "thread-list": "Needs the thread list, which lives in the desktop window's storage (threads, their search and the conversation archive). Follow-up: move the thread index into the backend, then add thread list/create/send/delete.",
    "webhook-ingress": "Called by outside services that fire a webhook, not by a user or script of this computer.",
    "phone-only": "A phone screen's own data (overview cards, drafts, file explorer, media, developer log). Scripts use the filesystem and the commands above.",
    "source-control": "Source control. Use git directly; wrapping it would be a second git.",
    "browser": "Controls Raticode's browser tabs, which need a display.",
    "window-settings": "App settings that the desktop window owns and applies. Most are UI preferences a script doesn't need.",
    "user-decision": "Your decision on an organization ticket: approve its plan, accept or send back its review, or reopen it. Each one lets agents start work. The CLI doesn't offer these yet; decide in the Organizations tab.",
    "protocol-reply": "Sent by the desktop to a phone: a reply, snapshot, progress update or error for one of the phone's requests. Nothing to call.",
    "device-link": "Belongs to the encrypted link between paired devices: syncing, file transfer, cancelling a phone's request and remote jobs sent to another desktop. A script on this computer uses the backend directly instead, for example `Raticode rem tasks create`.",
    "file-explorer": "The desktop window's file explorer, editor and project search. Scripts read and write project files directly.",
    "app-updates": "Updates the desktop app itself. Update the CLI with your package manager or a new release download."
  },
